  "summary": "I’m a Software Engineer with experience building scalable backend and cloud systems using C#, .NET, Azure, GraphQL, REST APIs, and PostgreSQL.\nAt Baxter International, I work across the full software development lifecycle—from architecture and proof-of-concept development to implementation, deployment, and production support. I’ve led feature development for hospital communication platforms, designed cloud-based solutions for cross-hospital data sharing, improved API and GraphQL performance, and built authentication and authorization systems using Keycloak and OpenID Connect.\nI enjoy solving complex engineering problems, especially those involving distributed systems, performance, data, and developer-facing architecture. Some of my work has reduced data retrieval times by 85%, decreased database transaction times by 50%, and reduced server resource utilization by 30%.\nOutside of my professional work, I have a strong interest in programming languages, compilers, and systems programming. I’ve built projects involving LLVM, Rust interpreters, and an OCaml compiler with type checking, dataflow analysis, and register allocation.\nI’m always interested in challenging engineering problems, learning new technologies, and building software that is reliable, performant, and useful to the people who depend on it.",
